/target
Cargo.lock
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*.rs.bk

# The third-party discovery test writes a tier directory under the crate it
# runs in and removes it again. An interrupted run leaves one behind.
widget-tiers*/

# === mockspace-managed build artifacts (do not edit) ===
# Catch-all: every cargo build dir, including nested ones under benches/,
# tests/, and research sketches. A leading-slash /target would miss those.
target/
# === end mockspace-managed build artifacts ===

# === mockspace-managed, regenerated by `cargo mock`; do not edit by hand ===
# The agent-integration outputs. Their sources are the templates under `mock/agent/`,
# plus mockspace's builtins where the repo overrides nothing.
/.claude/
/.github/copilot-instructions.md
/.github/hooks/
/.github/instructions/
/.github/skills/
# The TOML language-server binding. Derives from `mockspace.toml` and points at schemas
# under `target/`, so it says nothing a clone can use before a build.
/.taplo.toml
# === end mockspace-managed ===

# `docs/` is deliberately not ignored. It is the rendered design, generated from the
# `mock/*.md.tmpl` templates, and it is what a visitor reads.
